    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-concept-purpose-35": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-concept-purpose-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "| Concept | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| Epoch size | Total target admissions for one epoch. |\n| Worker pool size | Number of worker slots the run loop tries to keep active. |\n| Candidate window | Number of ranked board candidates scanned to satisfy admission. |"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-worker-pool-size-is-the-36": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-worker-pool-size-is-the-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Worker pool size is the consumer concurrency target, not the raw compiler parallelism target. Worker jobs can be running while expensive validation or tool calls wait behind per-epoch tool slots. The active epoch owns a fixed admitted target set, while the jobs table is the durable ready and execution queue for those targets."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-there-are-three-hot-path-37": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-there-are-three-hot-path-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "There are three hot-path capacity controls:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-control-owns-38": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-control-owns-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "| Control | Owns |\n| --- | --- |\n| Worker consumer pool | Number of worker jobs allowed to execute concurrently. |\n| Jobs table | Admitted worker slots ordered by priority DESC, created_at ASC, and job_id ASC, with durable claim and lease state. |\n| Tool/build slots | Number of concurrent compile-heavy validation and Pi tool operations allowed across worker worktrees in an epoch. |"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
