      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-an-epoch-target-plus-tar-49": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-an-epoch-target-plus-tar-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A worker job, its atomically acquired epoch target, and the resulting target claim form the bounded delegation contract. The host provisions the worktree, builds the TaskSpec, and writes task_spec.json before the executor starts job-runner worker-task --task-file …. The child receives target-local context, validation expectations, and a ClaimToken; it never claims queue work or receives the dispatch lease."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-the-scheduler-can-admit-50": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-the-scheduler-can-admit-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The scheduler can admit a previously attempted target into a later epoch only\nwhen deterministic routing has authority to do so, such as regression repair,\naccepted new facts, or explicit operator policy. Normal admission stays biased\ntoward fresh, graph-ranked work."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
